  "root_cause_correction": "The former attribution to missing dnsmasq.dns ACL was incomplete: the stock ubus jail shortcut binds the old socket inode, preventing reconnection even with the corrected ACL. A read-only socket-parent mount, exact ACL grant and runtime retry policy are all required.",
  "changes": [
    "Publish only exact dnsmasq and dnsmasq.dns for the dnsmasq user; preserve hotplug method permissions.",
    "Replace the init ubus jail shortcut with a read-only /var/run/ubus mount; preserve log jail, identity, capabilities and remaining mounts.",
    "Keep configured ubus name after runtime failures; retry on an explicit one-second poll deadline; bound logs per disconnection.",
    "Runtime HELLO and both registration requests share 100 ms, with STOP cancellation; initial startup registration remains fatal on error."
  ],
